  "interpretation_limits": [
    "Backpatch timings measure metadata insertion during compilation, not runtime faults. Rehash overlaps backpatch and compile spans; do not sum them. Elapsed spans include scheduler effects.",
    "Separate-run resident reuse counts are address membership comparisons, not deterministic paired execution; invalidated blocks are absent. Most matched burst blocks were reused, weakening the case for a first-visit-only interpreter tier. No tier implemented.",
    "131072-entry reservation did not remove growth and showed worse frame tails in its one comparison. Preserve this failed experiment.",
    "524288 requests produced 8192 buckets per shard and zero in-window growth events in the instrumented trial. This is scoped evidence, not a blanket claim that all future growth is removed.",
    "Muted Cubeb callbacks do not verify crackle-free audible output. No current visual or continuous-combat proof. Goal remains unmet."
  ],
  "decision": "Keep default-off. Eliminated measured in-window growth in one profiled test, but repeated frame-tail benefit was mixed/modest and >50ms frames remain. No major FPS gain or goal acceptance."
